IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pid-dates`
IMPORT `pid-disclosures`

-- Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (NSW) -- Part 5, receiving and dealing with voluntary public interest
-- disclosures, as it meets the discloser (ss 49, 59, 60, 61-62, 64, 65).
--
-- Questions: "Must the agency deal with my disclosure as a voluntary public interest disclosure?" (s 49), "By what day
-- must the agency give me my next progress update, and is it overdue?" (s 59(3), a regulative rule), "Can I apply for
-- internal review, and by what day?" (s 60, a regulative rule), "Can I recover damages from the agency for failing to
-- manage the risk of detrimental action?" (ss 61, 62), "Does the Act stop my identity being revealed?" (s 64), "Must I
-- help with an investigation?" (s 65).
--
-- Out: ss 50-58 (how agencies receive, refer and investigate; ss 50 and 55(3) appear as facts asked), s 63 (regulations),
-- s 66 (corrective action; it appears in pid-protections.l4 as the s 35(5) defence). Reasons in NOTES.md.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 30 October 2023; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not
-- for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 -- Part 5, dealing with voluntary public interest disclosures`

§§ `The nouns`

-- s 60(1) decisions open to internal review, and any other.
DECLARE `The decision I want reviewed` IS ONE OF
    `a decision that the agency need not deal with my disclosure as a voluntary public interest disclosure`
    `a decision to stop dealing with my disclosure as a voluntary public interest disclosure`
    `a decision neither to investigate nor to refer my disclosure`
    `a decision to stop investigating without completing the investigation or referring my disclosure`
    `some other decision`

-- s 64(2) the cases in which the ban on identifying information does not prevent disclosure, and none.
DECLARE `Why my identity would be revealed` IS ONE OF
    `I consented in writing`
    `it is generally known I made it because I voluntarily identified myself`
    `after consulting me, it is reasonably considered necessary to protect someone from detriment`
    `it is necessary to tell a person whose interests are affected by the disclosure`
    `it has already been lawfully published`
    `it is told to a medical practitioner or psychologist caring for or counselling me`
    `it is for proceedings before a court or tribunal`
    `it is necessary to deal with the disclosure effectively`
    `it is otherwise in the public interest`
    `none of these`

-- s 62(2): who pays damages under s 62.
DECLARE `Who pays under section 62` IS ONE OF
    `the agency`
    `the State`
    `no one, under section 62`

-- The parties and acts of the two regulative rules.
DECLARE `Dealing party` IS ONE OF `the agency`, `the discloser`
DECLARE `Dealing act` IS ONE OF
    `give the discloser a progress update`
    `apply for internal review`

§§ `s 49 -- the agency's duty to deal with the disclosure`

-- s 49(1) "An agency that receives a disclosure must deal with the disclosure as a voluntary public interest disclosure
-- ... if (a) the disclosure is a voluntary public interest disclosure, or (b) the disclosure is about serious wrongdoing
-- and is made by a person who is or appears to be a public official, but is not a mandatory public interest disclosure
-- or a witness public interest disclosure." s 49(2) the agency may cease if (a) it decides the disclosure is not a
-- voluntary public interest disclosure and (b) it is not in fact one. s 50: an agency receives a disclosure made or
-- communicated to its disclosure officer (asked as a fact).
@export Must the agency deal with (or keep dealing with) my disclosure as a voluntary public interest disclosure (s 49)?
GIVEN `the agency received my disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency received your disclosure: it was made or passed on to the head of the agency or another of its disclosure officers, referred to it, or otherwise communicated to it under a law, policy or arrangement
      `the kind of my disclosure` IS A `The kind of disclosure` @desc The kind of disclosure you made (see "What kind of public interest disclosure did I make"). One of: "a voluntary public interest disclosure", "a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency", "a witness public interest disclosure", "a mandatory public interest disclosure", "not a public interest disclosure"
      `it is about serious wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disclosure alleges or tends to show serious wrongdoing (see "Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing")
      `I am or appear to be a public official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, or appear to the agency to be, a public official
      `I made it as a witness or under a duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made it as part of your role, under a legal obligation, or at the request of an investigator (a mandatory or witness disclosure)
      `the agency decided it is not a voluntary disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency has decided your disclosure is not a voluntary public interest disclosure
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the agency deal with my disclosure as voluntary` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the agency received my disclosure`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 49 binds "an agency that receives a disclosure")
           IF `it is a voluntary public interest disclosure` `the kind of my disclosure` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 49(1)(a); s 49(2)(b) never met
           IF `limb (b)` AND (NOT `the agency decided it is not a voluntary disclosure`) THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 49(1) "if" not met, or s 49(2) cessation
    WHERE
        DECIDE `limb (b)` IF
                `it is about serious wrongdoing`
            AND `I am or appear to be a public official`
            AND (NOT `I made it as a witness or under a duty`)
            AND (NOT (`the kind of my disclosure` EQUALS `a mandatory public interest disclosure`))
            AND (NOT (`the kind of my disclosure` EQUALS `a witness public interest disclosure`))

§§ `s 59 -- what the agency must tell me`

-- s 59(1)-(2): an agency dealing with a voluntary public interest disclosure must give the maker access to its policy and
-- tell them, as soon as reasonably practicable, that Part 5 Division 2 applies, how it is dealing with the disclosure,
-- its reasons for a s 55(3) decision, referral details, progress updates, the results and corrective action.
-- s 59(3) "An agency is to provide updates on the progress of an investigation at intervals of not more than 3 months
-- throughout the duration of the investigation." Time 0 is the day of the last update (or, if none, the day the
-- investigation began, fork F7); the unit is days. s 59(5): none of this applies to an anonymous disclosure or to the
-- extent the maker waived the right in writing.
GIVEN `the days in three months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Dealing party` `Dealing act`
`s 59(3) -- the agency must give a progress update within three months` `the days in three months` MEANS
    PARTY `the agency`
    MUST `give the discloser a progress update`
    WITHIN `the days in three months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the agency` BECAUSE "no progress update within 3 months of the last one (s 59(3))"

@export By what day must the agency investigating my disclosure give me my next progress update (s 59(3))?
GIVEN `the day of the last update` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency last gave you an update on the progress of the investigation or, if it has given none, the day the investigation began
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I get my next progress update` MEANS `the day of the last update` `plus months` 3

@export Is the agency late with a progress update on its investigation of my voluntary public interest disclosure (s 59(3), (5))?
GIVEN `the kind of my disclosure` IS A `The kind of disclosure` @desc The kind of disclosure you made. One of: "a voluntary public interest disclosure", "a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency", "a witness public interest disclosure", "a mandatory public interest disclosure", "not a public interest disclosure"
      `my disclosure was anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disclosure was anonymous (there was no reasonably practicable way to communicate with you about it)
      `I waived in writing my right to information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you waived in writing your right to receive information from the agency
      `the investigation is still going` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency is still investigating the serious wrongdoing you disclosed
      `the day of the last update` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency last gave you a progress update or, if it has given none, the day the investigation began
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date (or the day you are asking about)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my progress update overdue` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`it is a voluntary public interest disclosure` `the kind of my disclosure`)) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 59 reaches only voluntary public interest disclosures)
           IF `my disclosure was anonymous` OR `I waived in writing my right to information` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 59(5) "do not apply"
           IF (NOT `the investigation is still going`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- "throughout the duration of the investigation"
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 59(3) -- the agency must give a progress update within three months` `the three months`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the agency` `give the discloser a progress update` `days to today`))
               WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST FALSE  -- an update today would still be in time
               OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the three months` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the last update` `to` (`the day of the last update` `plus months` 3)
        `days to today` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the last update` `to` `today`

§§ `s 60 -- internal review`

-- s 60(1) the maker may apply for internal review of (a) a decision that the agency is not required by s 49(1) to deal
-- with the disclosure as voluntary, (b) a decision under s 49(2) to cease, (c) a decision in s 55(3). s 60(2) the
-- application must (a) be made within 28 days after the day on which the applicant is informed of the decision, (b) be
-- in writing and state the applicant's reasons, (c) be dealt with by a reviewer not substantially involved. s 60(4)-(6):
-- the reviewer confirms, or decides the disclosure is to be dealt with as voluntary, and the agency gives effect to it.
-- Written as a rule (an opportunity, not a duty): the discloser applies within 28 days, counted from the day informed
-- (time 0); applying later takes the trace to BREACH, which here means only "out of time".
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Dealing party` `Dealing act`
`s 60(2)(a) -- the discloser applies for internal review within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the discloser`
    DO `apply for internal review`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the discloser` BECAUSE "the application for internal review was not made within 28 days after the day the applicant was informed of the decision (s 60(2)(a))"

@export By what day must I apply for internal review of the agency's decision about my disclosure (s 60(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the day I was told of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you were informed of the agency's decision
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I apply for internal review` MEANS `the day I was told of the decision` `plus days` 28

@export Can I apply for internal review of the agency's decision about my disclosure (s 60)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision I want reviewed` @desc The decision. One of: "a decision that the agency need not deal with my disclosure as a voluntary public interest disclosure", "a decision to stop dealing with my disclosure as a voluntary public interest disclosure", "a decision neither to investigate nor to refer my disclosure", "a decision to stop investigating without completing the investigation or referring my disclosure", "some other decision"
      `the day I was told of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you were informed of the decision
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply (or plan to apply) for internal review
      `my application is in writing with my reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application is in writing and states why you think the decision should not have been made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for internal review` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the decision` EQUALS `some other decision` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 60(1) names its decisions; others are outside its words)
           IF (NOT `my application is in writing with my reasons`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 60(2)(b) "must"
           IF `the day I was told of the decision` `is after` `the day I apply` THEN JUST TRUE  -- applying before being told is not out of time
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 60(2)(a) -- the discloser applies for internal review within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the discloser` `apply for internal review` (`the days from` `the day I was told of the decision` `to` `the day I apply`)))
               WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
               OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- a period fixed in the Act's own words

§§ `ss 61, 62 -- the agency's liability for failing to manage the risk`

-- s 61(1) a "responsible agency" for a voluntary public interest disclosure is one (a) aware it has been made (a
-- disclosure officer is aware, or ought reasonably to be, s 61(3)) and (b) to which (i) the disclosure relates, or (ii)
-- whose associated public official is known to be the maker. s 61(2) it must take steps to assess and minimise the risk
-- of detrimental action (other than reasonable management action) against the maker, the subject of the disclosure and
-- others. s 62(1) a person who suffers injury, damage or loss as a result of the failure may recover damages, (2) from
-- the agency if it is a person, otherwise from the State; (3) the defendant must prove compliance, or that the loss was
-- not caused by the failure; (4) exemplary damages; (5) not also under ICAC Act s 79J, Ombudsman Act s 31S or LECC Act
-- s 97I; (6) compensation already received under s 35 is taken into account. Fork F8: where the agency is not a
-- responsible agency, NOTHING.
@export Can I recover damages because the agency failed to manage the risk of detrimental action over a voluntary public interest disclosure, and from whom (ss 61, 62)?
GIVEN `the kind of the disclosure` IS A `The kind of disclosure` @desc The kind of the disclosure in question (yours, or one about you). One of: "a voluntary public interest disclosure", "a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency", "a witness public interest disclosure", "a mandatory public interest disclosure", "not a public interest disclosure"
      `the agency knew or ought to have known of the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a disclosure officer for the agency knew, or ought reasonably to have known, that the disclosure had been made
      `the disclosure relates to the agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disclosure is about serious wrongdoing by the agency or one of its officials, or affecting its functions
      `the maker is known to be associated with the agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the maker of the disclosure is known to be a public official associated with the agency (employed by it, in its service, or a contractor or volunteer for it)
      `I suffered injury, damage or loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered injury, damage or loss
      `the agency proved it took steps to assess and minimise the risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency (or the State) has proved it did take steps to assess and minimise the risk of detrimental action
      `the agency proved my loss was not caused by its failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency (or the State) has proved your injury, damage or loss was not the result of its failure
      `I already recovered damages for it under another integrity Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already recovered damages for the same detrimental action under ICAC Act s 79J, Ombudsman Act s 31S or LECC Act s 97I
      `the agency is a legal person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency is itself a legal person (for example a council or a statutory corporation); a Public Service department or a group of staff usually is not
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who pays under section 62`
`Who pays me damages under section 62` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`it is a voluntary public interest disclosure` `the kind of the disclosure`)) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 61 reaches voluntary public interest disclosures)
           IF (NOT `the agency knew or ought to have known of the disclosure`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (not a responsible agency; fork F8)
           IF (NOT `the disclosure relates to the agency`) AND (NOT `the maker is known to be associated with the agency`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (fork F8)
           IF (NOT `I suffered injury, damage or loss`) THEN JUST `no one, under section 62`
           IF `the agency proved it took steps to assess and minimise the risk` THEN JUST `no one, under section 62`
           IF `the agency proved my loss was not caused by its failure` THEN JUST `no one, under section 62`
           IF `I already recovered damages for it under another integrity Act` THEN JUST `no one, under section 62`  -- s 62(5) "not entitled"
           IF `the agency is a legal person` THEN JUST `the agency`
           OTHERWISE JUST `the State`

§§ `s 64 -- my identity`

-- s 64(1) "Information tending to identify a person as the maker of a voluntary public interest disclosure ... is not
-- to be disclosed by a public official or an agency." s 64(2) "does not prevent" disclosure in (a)-(i). s 64(3): making
-- a disclosure in confidence is not voluntary self-identification. s 64(4): the ICAC, Ombudsman and LECC Acts prevail;
-- s 64(5): other restrictions still apply. Fork F9: the answer is about s 64 alone.
@export Does the Act stop a public official or agency revealing that I made my voluntary public interest disclosure (s 64)?
GIVEN `the kind of my disclosure` IS A `The kind of disclosure` @desc The kind of disclosure you made. One of: "a voluntary public interest disclosure", "a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency", "a witness public interest disclosure", "a mandatory public interest disclosure", "not a public interest disclosure"
      `why it would be revealed` IS A `Why my identity would be revealed` @desc Why your identity would be revealed. One of: "I consented in writing", "it is generally known I made it because I voluntarily identified myself" (making it in confidence is not identifying yourself), "after consulting me, it is reasonably considered necessary to protect someone from detriment", "it is necessary to tell a person whose interests are affected by the disclosure", "it has already been lawfully published", "it is told to a medical practitioner or psychologist caring for or counselling me", "it is for proceedings before a court or tribunal", "it is necessary to deal with the disclosure effectively", "it is otherwise in the public interest", "none of these"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does section 64 stop my identity being revealed` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`it is a voluntary public interest disclosure` `the kind of my disclosure`))
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 64 protects the maker of a voluntary public interest disclosure)
    ELSE IF `why it would be revealed` EQUALS `none of these`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 64(1) "is not to be disclosed"
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 64(2) "does not prevent"

§§ `s 65 -- my duty to assist an investigation`

-- s 65 "A public official must use the public official's best endeavours to assist in an investigation of serious
-- wrongdoing if asked to do so by a person dealing with a voluntary public interest disclosure on behalf of an agency."
-- Note: doing so is a witness public interest disclosure, protected by Part 3.
@export Must I use my best endeavours to help with an investigation of serious wrongdoing (s 65)?
GIVEN `I am a public official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a public official (see "Am I a public official")
      `I was asked by someone dealing with a disclosure for an agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person dealing with a voluntary public interest disclosure on behalf of an agency asked you to help with the investigation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I help with the investigation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am a public official`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 65 binds public officials; the investigator's own Act may bind others)
    ELSE IF `I was asked by someone dealing with a disclosure for an agency`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- "if asked"
